    "name": "Kale Raab",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Kale raab is&nbsp;the tender, flowering shoot that emerges from overwintered kale plants in early spring, offering a sweet, nutty, and slightly bitter flavor, and is a nutritious part of the brassica family, rich in vitamins A, C, and K. It's a seasonal delicacy often harvested before the yellow flowers fully open, and can be eaten raw in salads or cooked by sautéing, roasting, or adding to pasta, soups, and frittatas, typically with garlic, olive oil, and lemon juice.&nbsp;</span></p>",
